To validate props in React, developers use **PropTypes**. They provide runtime type checking during development.

#### Usage example:

```jsx
import PropTypes from 'prop-types';

function UserCard({ name, age }) {
  return <div>{name} ({age})</div>;
}

UserCard.propTypes = {
  name: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
  age: PropTypes.number,
};
```

PropTypes are checked only in development mode and do not enforce types at runtime in production.

answer.uk:
